hexagon: reject a GDN conv chain when its slot stride is less than a slot
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-fusion/0007-hexagon-htp-gdn-fusions-with-rollback-slots.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

With rollback snapshots, the GDN conv chain writes one row of the conv
cache into each snapshot slot. The fused op writes the slots from one base
address and one stride. The matcher takes the distance between two
adjacent slots as the stride, but it did not compare that stride with the
size of a slot. Thus it accepted slots with an overlap, for example two
slots 144 bytes apart with a slot of 288 bytes. The DSP rejects such a
stride with the status 4, and the compute of the graph then fails.

This patch rejects the fused op when the stride is less than the size of a
slot. The chain then stays with the unfused ops, and each CPY writes its
own slot.

On the model graphs of the app, the stride of the snapshot slots is equal
to the size of a slot, on the 2B and on the 4B. Thus the decode path with
4 snapshots fuses the conv step as before. hexhost_graphs gives the same
ops with and without this patch on the decode, prefill, MTP and image
paths. The check is one comparison when a graph is new to the graph cache.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
index 76827fc..910dcaa 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
@@ -423,6 +423,11 @@ static inline const char * ggml_hexagon_gdn_conv_chain_check(const ggml_cgraph *
             }
         }
     }
+    // The fused op writes the slots from one base and one stride, and the DSP rejects a stride that
+    // is less than the size of a slot. Thus slots with an overlap stay with the unfused ops.
+    if (n_slots > 1 && stride < (size_t) row * sizeof(float)) {
+        return "the slot stride is less than a slot";
+    }
 
     ggml_tensor * P    = cpys[0];
     ggml_tensor * last = P->src[0];
